{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1105130-increasing-your-size-with-magic","id":1105130,"title":"Increasing your size with magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-18T12:23:27-07:00","id":1105130,"title":"Increasing your size with magic","content":"I assume that mages without problems could use a Life Weaving spell to outright increase their size equal to Potency, which makes me want to pose a couple of questions:<br /> <br /> 1) Would such a spell completely ignore the square-cube law? By all rights, suddenly gaining so much more mass should make the mage collapse under their own weight. I guess I can just do the &quot;Oh well, it's magic&quot;-thing and shrug, but at the same time I wonder if it would be better to subject the mage to the square-cube law past a certain size (maybe past 6) and having to expend a Reach to ignore this limitation and grow as much as your Potency can afford.<br /> <br /> 2) What would more size mean mechanically? Obviously you will increase in Health and Speed, your clothes will rip to shreds and spell factors and fighting styles to overcome your size will be affected accordingly. But when you are so big you should also be rather unwieldy and easy to hit, giving you penalties to Defense past a certain size. Also, having so much mass would surely increase the heft in your attacks, giving you some sort of damage bonus as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T14:05:17-07:00","id":1105172,"title":"","content":"Since the maximum of a mortal is size 6 I can agree with reach to go further as a human just as is requires for going beyond 5 dots in a skill or attribute. But for the science side of it I'd say the answer is &quot;magic&quot;.<br /> <br /> As to mechanical benefits/penalties size really only effects health and a few other things. If you wanted the spell to do additional effects that fit thematically you could but it wouldn't be strictly from the size increase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T01:01:20-07:00","id":1105306,"title":"","content":"Long story short?<br /> Increasing your size is possible with Magic, and ignores most scientific laws.<br /> Inverse square law ceases to function, you don't need to think about all the stress it will put on your heart, and your punches deal no more damage than they previously did.<br /> <br /> Mages modify symbols by default, and unless you want to use those symbols to hard-code a new physical form for yourself that follows fallen laws (Patterning, 4 dots), then you're just patching your existing code (Weaving, 3 dots), with rules exceptions built into fallen laws so things that rationally make no sense still function. It's why you can increase your strength without changing your biology in any noticable way. It's why you can grant yourself venom without an understanding of how venom actually works.<br /> <br /> And it's why Magic worked properly throughout history, when people believed in the luminiferous aether, phlogiston, the philosopher's stone, and biological humors.<br /> Things which we now know to be rubbish.<br /> <br /> That is, assuming those things haven't been introduced through some Archmaster/Ascended Mage's tomfoolery in the Supernal Realms.<br /> <br /> Long story even shorter?<br /> Weaving is rules exceptions, which can easily violate scientific laws.<br /> Patterning is re-defining, which while still &quot;impossible&quot; can sit neater alongside conventional science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","user":"HerbertIsBestBert","date":". 06-19-2017, 04:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T01:12:59-07:00","id":1105309,"title":"","content":"<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1105130-increasing-your-size-with-magic#post1105130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would such a spell completely ignore the square-cube law? By all rights, suddenly gaining so much more mass should make the mage collapse under their own weight. I guess I can just do the &quot;Oh well, it's magic&quot;-thing and shrug, but at the same time I wonder if it would be better to subject the mage to the square-cube law past a certain size (maybe past 6) and having to expend a Reach to ignore this limitation and grow as much as your Potency can afford.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that a published spell for this already exists, doesn't require Reach to invalidate the square-cube law, or for going past Size 6, I don't think there's going to be any issues for this.<br /> <br /> Ironically, as-written, it requires both Matter &amp; Life, which is weird.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1105130-increasing-your-size-with-magic#post1105130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume that mages without problems could use a Life Weaving spell to outright increase their size equal to Potency, which makes me want to pose a couple of questions:<br /> 2) What would more size mean mechanically? Obviously you will increase in Health and Speed,</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW? That's about it.<br /> <br /> If you want to look at house rules for more, I'd look at various threads for Mecha or the Colossal Form Dread Power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 06-19-2017, 04:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T04:03:11-07:00","id":1105334,"title":"","content":"I assume the Matter+Life version of Shrink and Grow is for affecting a target and their clothes without the use of a combined spell. Life ought to be assumed capable of an inverted version of the spell in much the same way that many of the Death/Mind/Spirit spells do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T05:14:31-07:00","id":1105341,"title":"","content":"Or you could just use Space...you know, the arcanum of dimensions? The Secret Room spell is pretty much exactly what you're looking for, presuming you don't need to be stronger or faster with your increased size.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}